RISC OS: at most 100 main-loop passes a second.

A screen that draws little or nothing (the "release the keys" wait before
a flight, the menu between redraws) went round the loop thousands of times
a second with no sleep (the Pi log showed 5812 loops in 5 s). If a pass
takes under 10 ms, FsSleep (Wimp_PollIdle) gives the rest back to the
desktop. A game frame takes far longer, so flying is not slowed.

For ysce_public 1b13297, after 08-riscos-timing. See docs/PORTING-NOTES.md in riscos-ysflight.

--- a/src/fslazywindow/src/linux_win/fslazywindow.cpp
+++ b/src/fslazywindow/src/linux_win/fslazywindow.cpp
@@ -191,6 +191,16 @@
 			FsSleep(sleepMS-(int)passed);
 		}
 #ifdef __riscos__
+		/* At most 100 loops a second: a screen that draws nothing (e.g.
+		   waiting for the keys to be released before a flight) would
+		   otherwise take all the CPU. A game frame takes far longer. */
+		{
+			long long spent=FsSubSecondTimer()-m0;
+			if(spent<10)
+			{
+				FsSleep((int)(10-spent));
+			}
+		}
 		long long m4=FsSubSecondTimer();
 		tSleep+=m4-m3;
 		if(5000<=m4-tReport && 0<nFrame)
